## Analytical Approach

The project followed a structured Business Analytics workflow.

### 1. Data Quality & Validation

The dataset was reviewed for:

- Missing values
- Data types
- Transaction structure
- Fraud indicators
- Data consistency

### 2. Transaction & Fraud Exposure

Key metrics were calculated to understand:

- Total transaction volume
- Fraudulent transaction volume
- Overall fraud rate
- Total transaction value
- Fraudulent transaction value
- Average fraudulent transaction amount

### 3. Transaction-Type Analysis

Fraud activity was compared across:

- CASH-IN
- CASH-OUT
- DEBIT
- PAYMENT
- TRANSFER

This helped identify transaction types requiring greater monitoring attention.

### 4. Transaction Amount Analysis

Transactions were grouped into value bands to evaluate whether fraud risk changes with transaction size.

### 5. Time-Based Analysis

Fraud activity was analysed by:

- Hour of day
- Time period
- Transaction activity patterns

### 6. Monitoring Effectiveness

The existing fraud-monitoring flag was evaluated using:

- True Positives
- False Negatives
- False Positives
- True Negatives
- Detection Rate
- Missed Fraud Rate

### 7. Business Recommendations

The findings were translated into recommendations for:

- Risk-based monitoring
- Transaction prioritisation
- Fraud-rule enhancement
- Investigation workflows

