## Key Insights

### 01 — Transfer transactions represent a key fraud-risk area

**TRANSFER transactions demonstrated the highest fraud rate**, making them a priority area for enhanced transaction monitoring and risk-based controls.

### 02 — Fraud is concentrated in specific transaction types

Fraudulent activity is concentrated primarily within **TRANSFER and CASH-OUT transactions**, highlighting money-outflow activity as an important area of fraud risk.

### 03 — Existing monitoring misses substantial simulated fraud

The existing fraud-flagging mechanism captures only a small proportion of simulated fraudulent transactions, resulting in a substantial number of missed fraud cases.

This indicates an opportunity to improve the existing monitoring approach.

### 04 — Risk-based monitoring can improve investigation efficiency

Fraud exposure is not evenly distributed across transactions. Prioritising transactions according to factors such as transaction type, transaction value, and behavioural patterns can help focus investigation resources on higher-risk activity.

